  "name": "Adaptation of Computer Use Agents to New Software with User Manuals",
  "notes": "Reviewed the complete retained abstract and selected exact-v1 methods, evaluation and validation sections. Execution plans stay fixed per episode; policy training is separate and application-specific. Screenshot-based training/Slack judgments can miss task conditions, and OSWorld tasks may overlap backbone pretraining. No independent reproduction, safe-deployment guarantee or artifact-release verification.",
  "published_at": "2026-10-16",
  "relations": [],
  "review_status": "curated",
  "scope": "core",
  "summary": "MAGE retrieves software-manual sections into fixed execution plans and generates setup/main task-plan pairs whose GUI rollouts support application-specific policy adaptation with round-based GRPO.",
